    "Derivation": {
      "description": "A check's worked calculation: formula, substitution, result, citation.\n\n``symbolic`` is the governing formula written the way the source writes it\n(``\"σ_b = M · c / I\"``); ``inputs`` supply every symbol on its right-hand side;\n``result`` is the left-hand side with the computed value; and ``citation`` names\nthe handbook section or standard clause the formula comes from. Every symbol\nused carries its own glossary line, so the derivation is readable without the\nsource book open.",
      "properties": {
        "citation": {
          "title": "Citation",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "inputs": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/SymbolValue"
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "title": "Inputs",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "result": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/SymbolValue"
        },
        "symbolic": {
          "title": "Symbolic",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "symbolic",
        "inputs",
        "result",
        "citation"
      ],
      "title": "Derivation",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "DerivationAbsence": {
      "description": "Why a check renders no worked calculation — the two kinds that are finished.\n\nNeither is a shortfall. A ``LOOKUP`` has no arithmetic between its two numbers:\nan exemption, an identification line, a table comparison, a consistency verdict.\nA ``NUMERIC_RESULT`` has real mathematics behind it and no substitutable line —\nits value is the root of an equation, solved rather than evaluated, so the\ninputs/outputs table is the correct rendering for it rather than a shortfall.\n\nThe third kind a check can be in — **debt**, a closed form nobody has written\ndown yet — is deliberately not a member. Debt is the *absence* of a declaration,\nrecorded per clause in ``docs/api/underived-checks.txt`` where the ratchet keeps\nthe list downward-only. Making it declarable here would let a check retire its\nown debt by describing it, which is the collapse this vocabulary exists to refuse.",
      "enum": [
        "lookup",
        "numeric_result"
      ],
      "title": "DerivationAbsence",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "Direction": {
      "description": "Which way a parameter has to move to improve a check's margin.",
      "enum": [
        "increase",
        "decrease"
      ],
      "title": "Direction",
      "type": "string"
    },
